{"title":"Career Roadmap · Journalist","role":"Journalist","summary":"A Journalist researches, verifies, investigates, and communicates news and public-interest information through newspapers, digital publications, television, radio, podcasts, newsletters, and other media platforms. A Political Science background is particularly useful for political journalism, public policy, governance, elections, international affairs, and investigative reporting.","facts":{"Current degree":"BA (Bachelor of Arts - General / Honours)","Course":"Political Science"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Typical Timeline","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Foundation"},{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Politics, society, research and writing"}],[{"text":"Skill Building"},{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Reporting, interviewing and fact-checking"}],[{"text":"Specialisation"},{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Political/public-affairs journalism"}],[{"text":"Entry"},{"text":"Year 3–4"},{"text":"Journalism Intern / Junior Reporter"}],[{"text":"Early Career"},{"text":"1–3 years"},{"text":"Reporting and news production"}],[{"text":"Mid Career"},{"text":"3–6 years"},{"text":"Beat reporting and investigative work"}],[{"text":"Senior"},{"text":"6–10 years"},{"text":"Senior Correspondent / Editor"}],[{"text":"Management"},{"text":"8–15 years"},{"text":"Bureau/Desk/Newsroom leadership"}],[{"text":"Leadership"},{"text":"15+ years"},{"text":"Editor / Editorial Director / Media Leadership"}]]}]},{"heading":"What to Build Each Year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build This","Key Skills","Proof"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Political & social foundation"},{"text":"Political theory, current affairs, research"},{"text":"Analytical articles"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Journalism fundamentals"},{"text":"Reporting, interviewing, fact-checking"},{"text":"Published clips"}],[{"text":"Year